// §A3 follow-up (§10.5) — `Ptr[T].value` / `MutPtr[T].value`
// dereference.
//
// `Ptr[T]` and `MutPtr[T]` came from §A3 as the raw-mint
// primitive that admits an external integer address into the
// type system under the `RawMemory` capability. Their first
// slice typed pointers but didn't ship a Vestra source-level
// way to read or write through them — code that needed the
// pointee value had to route through `Span.raw(at: p, count:
// 1)` and index 0, or hand the pointer off to a foreign
// function that did the dereference. This slice closes that
// gap.
//
// The spelling is `.value`, the same shape Box[T] already
// uses for "extract the inner". For Ptr[T] the result is
// the read-only T; for MutPtr[T] it's a writable T (the
// `p.value = expr` shape is admitted as an assign-through).
// Both lower to a plain `(*p)` at the C++ layer — the
// existing `reinterpret_cast<T*>(addr)` from §A3 mints a
// pointer with the right type, and `*` reads / writes it.
//
// Dereferencing doesn't require an additional capability
// because the `.unchecked(fromAddress:)` mint already
// discharged `RawMemory`. The audit lane covering the mint
// also covers the reads / writes — a `vestra audit
// --raw-memory` walk lands every `.value`-on-Ptr / MutPtr
// alongside the mint that produced the pointer.

module examples.ptr_deref

// Read a UInt32 from a raw address.
func load_word(_ addr: UInt64) -> UInt32 {
    with RawMemory {
        let p: Ptr[UInt32] = Ptr.unchecked(fromAddress: addr)
        return p.value
    }
}

// Write a UInt32 to a raw address.
func store_word(_ addr: UInt64, _ v: UInt32) {
    with RawMemory {
        let p: MutPtr[UInt32] = MutPtr.unchecked(fromAddress: addr)
        p.value = v
    }
}

// Read-modify-write through a single MutPtr — the kernel's
// "atomic-style" non-atomic update path. The compiler emits
// two distinct memory operations; if the user needs a real
// atomic RMW they reach for §A4's Atomic[T] instead.
func bump_word(_ addr: UInt64, _ delta: UInt32) -> UInt32 {
    with RawMemory {
        let p: MutPtr[UInt32] = MutPtr.unchecked(fromAddress: addr)
        p.value = p.value + delta
        return p.value
    }
}
